
  SUPERSINGULARITY AND META-PATTERNS

======================================================================

  I. SUPERSINGULARITY: THE CONCEPT
  --------------------------------------------------

  ORDINARY: Frobenius has distinct eigenvalues. Structure 'spread out'.
  SUPERSINGULAR: Frobenius eigenvalues collapse. Maximum symmetry.

  Examples:
  - Formal group: [p](x) = 0 over F_p (height = infinity)
  - Elliptic curve: E[p] = 0 (no p-torsion)
  - End(E) = maximal order in QUATERNION ALGEBRA (not commutative)
  - K3 surface: formal Brauer group has infinite height

  The pattern: supersingular = the prime p is TOTALLY ABSORBED.
  Nothing survives reduction mod p. The algebra becomes quaternionic.
  This is the arithmetic analogue of a BLACK HOLE.

